/-
# Problem Description (Stacks Project Lemma 15.40.2, tag 07NM)

Throughout, "ring" means commutative ring with unit, and a local ring `(R, m)` is a
ring with a unique maximal ideal `m`. We write `kappa = R/m` for its residue field.

Let `K` be a field and let `A = K[[x_1, ..., x_n]]` (the formal power series ring in
`n` variables over `K`). Let `Lambda` be a Cohen ring (a complete discrete valuation
ring whose uniformizer is a prime number `p`), and let `B = Lambda[[x_1, ..., x_n]]`.

`A` is a complete regular local ring of dimension `n` with maximal ideal
`m_A = (x_1, ..., x_n)` and residue field `K`. `B` is a complete regular local ring of
dimension `n+1` with maximal ideal `m_B = (p, x_1, ..., x_n)`.

The lemma asserts:

(1) If `y_1, ..., y_n` is a regular system of parameters of `A`, then the unique
    continuous `K`-algebra homomorphism `K[[Y_1, ..., Y_n]] -> A`, `Y_i -> y_i`, is an
    isomorphism.

(2) If `z_1, ..., z_r` form part of a regular system of parameters for `A`, then `r <= n`
    and `A/(z_1, ..., z_r) = K[[Y_1, ..., Y_{n-r}]]`.

(3) If `p, y_1, ..., y_n` is a regular system of parameters of `B`, then the unique
    continuous `Lambda`-algebra homomorphism `Lambda[[Y_1, ..., Y_n]] -> B`, `Y_i -> y_i`,
    is an isomorphism.

(4) If `p, z_1, ..., z_r` form part of a regular system of parameters for `B`, then
    `r <= n` and `B/(z_1, ..., z_r) = Lambda[[Y_1, ..., Y_{n-r}]]`.
-/

-- # Background and context (as comments)
--
-- Power series ring `K[[x_1, ..., x_n]]` is formalized as `MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K`,
-- with the variables given by `MvPowerSeries.X i` for `i : Fin n`.
--
-- A "Cohen ring" (Definition 4, Stacks 0327) is formalized by the existing predicate
-- `IsCohenRing`: a complete (`IsAdicComplete`) discrete valuation ring whose maximal
-- ideal is generated by a prime number `p`.
--
-- The "cotangent space" `m/m^2` (as a vector space over the residue field) is
-- `IsLocalRing.CotangentSpace R = (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).Cotangent`, and the
-- map `m -> m/m^2` is `(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).toCotangent`.
--
-- The "isomorphisms" of (1) and (3) are stated ON THE CANONICAL SUBSTITUTION MAP
-- `Y_i ↦ y_i` itself, not as the existence of some equivalence matching it on the
-- variables. For (1) that map is Mathlib's `MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom` and the assertion is
-- that it is bijective. For (3) the `y_i` may have nonzero constant coefficient (lying in
-- `m_Λ`), and Mathlib's `HasSubst` — which demands a *nilpotent* constant coefficient —
-- does not apply; the canonical map is then built by hand as `cohenSubstAlgHom`: the
-- `m_Λ`-adic translation by the constant terms followed by the substitution of the
-- normalized (zero-constant-coefficient) parts. The assertion is again that this map is
-- bijective. Both statements also record that the map sends `X i` to `y i`.

open IsLocalRing MvPowerSeries Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters

/-
================================================================================
# PROOF SKETCH OVERVIEW (Stacks 07NM)

The four statements are powered by TWO ENGINES, each the isomorphism statement (1)
resp. (3), plus bookkeeping lemmas for the cardinality bound and the quotient-by-
initial-variables identification used in (2)/(4).

`A := MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K`,  `B := MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ`.

Engine 1 (over a field K) supports statements (1) and (2).
Engine 2 (over a Cohen ring Λ) supports statements (3) and (4).

The comparison map of statement (1) is, concretely:
  `φ := MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom (h : HasSubst y) : K[[Y]] →ₐ[K] A`,  `φ (X i) = y i`,
where `HasSubst y` holds because each `y i` lies in `m_A`, hence has zero constant
coefficient (`MvPowerSeries.hasSubst_of_constantCoeff_zero`, valid since `Fin n` is
finite).  `φ` is shown to be bijective; the desired `AlgEquiv` is `AlgEquiv.ofBijective φ`.

The mathematical content (all four claims SANITY CHECKED — no counterexamples found):
  * (1a) surjectivity: the `y_i` generate `m_A` modulo `m_A^2`, hence generate `m_A` by
    (topological) Nakayama; completeness of `A` then upgrades "generates `m_A`" to
    surjectivity of `φ` by successive approximation (Stacks 0G1V style).
  * (1b) injectivity: `K[[Y]]` and `A` are regular local DOMAINS of the same Krull
    dimension `n`; a surjection `φ : R ↠ S = R/ker φ` with `R` a domain and
    `dim S = dim R` forces `ker φ = 0`, because any nonzero `f ∈ ker φ ⊆ m_R` is a
    nonzerodivisor (R domain) so `dim R/(f) ≤ dim R − 1`, contradicting `dim S = dim R`.
    (The DOMAIN hypothesis on the source is load-bearing: e.g. `k[x,y]/(xy) ↠ k[x]` is a
    dimension-preserving surjection of local rings that is not injective — the source is
    not a domain. So injectivity must be derived via the explicit dimension-drop
    argument, NOT a generic "equal-dim domains" slogan.)

Engine 2 is identical with `Λ` (Cohen ⇒ complete) replacing `K`, with one subtlety
(SANITY CHECKED): the map `ψ : Λ[[Y]] →ₐ[Λ] B` is a `Λ`-algebra map, so the uniformizer
`p ∈ Λ` is sent to `p ∈ B` automatically (it is "used up" as a coefficient, NOT as a
`Y`-variable). Surjectivity of `ψ` requires that `p` TOGETHER WITH the `y_i` generate
`m_B`, which is exactly the hypothesis that `(p, y_1, …, y_n)` is a regular system of
parameters of `B` (length `n+1 = dim B`); the `y_i` alone do not generate `m_B`.
`dim Λ[[Y_1..Y_n]] = dim Λ + n = 1 + n = n+1 = dim B`, and both residue fields are
`Λ/(p)`.

BACKEND NOTE.  This `stacks` Mathlib backend is THIN on the deep commutative-algebra
infrastructure for `MvPowerSeries (Fin n)`:
  * `IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K)` — AVAILABLE (instance).
  * `IsNoetherianRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K)` — NOT available (even `Fin 0`).
  * `IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal …) (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K)` — NOT available.
  * Krull dimension `= n`, regularity, cotangent `finrank = n` — NOT available by name.
The substitution map API (`HasSubst`, `substAlgHom`, `substAlgHom_X`,
`hasSubst_of_constantCoeff_zero`) IS available and is used to build the comparison maps.
The missing infrastructure facts are supplied by the imported namespace
  `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters`
(`StacksDraft.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.{CotangentSpace, AdicTranslation,
InverseFunction}`): the two engines, the cotangent-space dimension computations, and the
quotient-by-initial-variables identifications used below.
================================================================================
-/

-- # Main Statement(s)

/-- **Statement (1).** If `y_1, ..., y_n` is a regular system of parameters of
`A = K[[x_1, ..., x_n]]`, then the canonical substitution map
`K[[Y_1, ..., Y_n]] → A`, `Y_i ↦ y_i`, is an isomorphism.

The canonical map is `MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom (hasSubst_of_mem_maximalIdeal y)`: the
substitution `X i ↦ y i`, which is defined precisely because each `y i` lies in `m_A` and
hence has zero constant coefficient, and which is the unique continuous `K`-algebra map
sending `X i` to `y i`. The conclusion states that *this* map sends `X i` to `y i` and is
bijective — i.e. is an isomorphism of `K`-algebras. -/
@[stacks 07NM "(1)",
  sga "1 II 4.14" "special case",
  sga "1 III 2.3" "special case",
  sga "2 IV 5.5" "special case",
  sga "3 VIIB 5.5.2" "partial"]
theorem main_theorem_one (K : Type*) [Field K] (n : ℕ)
    (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K)) (hy : IsRegularSystemOfParameters y) :
    (∀ i,
        (MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom (hasSubst_of_mem_maximalIdeal y) :
            MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K →ₐ[K] MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K)
          (MvPowerSeries.X i) = (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K)) ∧
      Function.Bijective
        ((MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom (hasSubst_of_mem_maximalIdeal y) :
          MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K →ₐ[K] MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K)) := by
  -- The comparison map `φ = substAlgHom : K[[Y]] →ₐ[K] A`, `X i ↦ y i`, sends `X i` to
  -- `y i` by `substAlgHom_X` and is bijective by Engine 1 (`engine_one_injective` +
  -- `engine_one_surjective`).
  refine ⟨fun i => ?_, ⟨engine_one_injective y hy, engine_one_surjective y hy⟩⟩
  simpa using MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom_X (hasSubst_of_mem_maximalIdeal y) i

/-- Statement (1) repackaged as an automorphism: the canonical map, being bijective, is a
`K`-algebra automorphism of `A` carrying `X i` to `y i`. This existential form is strictly
weaker than `main_theorem_one` (it forgets which map it is); it is the form in which
statement (2) consumes (1). -/
theorem exists_algEquiv_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters (K : Type*) [Field K] (n : ℕ)
    (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K)) (hy : IsRegularSystemOfParameters y) :
    ∃ e : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K ≃ₐ[K] MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K,
      ∀ i, e (MvPowerSeries.X i) = (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K) :=
  ⟨AlgEquiv.ofBijective _ (main_theorem_one K n y hy).2, (main_theorem_one K n y hy).1⟩

/-- If an automorphism `e` of `R[[x_1,…,x_n]]` sends `X i` to the `i`-th term of
`(z_1,…,z_r, w_1,…,w_{n-r})`, then the quotient by `(z_1,…,z_r)` is `R[[Y_1,…,Y_{n-r}]]`. -/
private theorem nonempty_quotient_algEquiv_of_algEquiv_X {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {n r : ℕ} (hr : r ≤ n) (z : Fin r → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R))
    (w : Fin (n - r) → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R))
    (he : ∃ e : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R ≃ₐ[R] MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R, ∀ i,
      e (MvPowerSeries.X i) =
        ((Fin.append z w ∘ Fin.cast (by omega : n = r + (n - r))) i :
          MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R)) :
    Nonempty
      ((MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R ⧸
          Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i => (z i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R)))) ≃ₐ[R]
        MvPowerSeries (Fin (n - r)) R) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := he
  -- Key fact: the `castLE hr i`-th term of `z ++ w` is `z i`.
  have hyz : ∀ i : Fin r,
      e (MvPowerSeries.X (Fin.castLE hr i)) = (z i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R) := by
    intro i
    rw [he, Function.comp_apply]
    have hidx : Fin.cast (by omega : n = r + (n - r)) (Fin.castLE hr i) = Fin.castAdd (n - r) i :=
      Fin.ext (by simp)
    rw [hidx, Fin.append_left]
  set A := MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R
  set I : Ideal A := Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i => (z i : A))) with hI_def
  set J : Ideal A :=
    Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i : Fin r => (MvPowerSeries.X (Fin.castLE hr i) : A))) with hJ_def
  -- `J = Ideal.map e.symm I`.
  have hJI : J = Ideal.map (e.symm : A →ₐ[R] A) I := by
    rw [hI_def, Ideal.map_span, hJ_def]
    congr 1
    rw [← Set.range_comp]
    apply congrArg
    funext i
    simp only [Function.comp_apply]
    rw [← hyz i]
    exact (AlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply e _).symm
  obtain ⟨f⟩ := quotient_initial_vars (R := R) (n := n) (r := r) hr
  exact ⟨(Ideal.quotientEquivAlg I J (e.symm : A ≃ₐ[R] A) hJI).trans f⟩

/-- **Statement (2).** If `z_1, ..., z_r` form part of a regular system of parameters for
`A = K[[x_1, ..., x_n]]`, then `r <= n` and `A/(z_1, ..., z_r)` is isomorphic (as a
`K`-algebra) to the power series ring `K[[Y_1, ..., Y_{n-r}]]`. -/
@[stacks 07NM "(2)", ega "0 17.1.4" "more general", ega "0 17.1.7" "special case"]
theorem main_theorem_two (K : Type*) [Field K] (n r : ℕ)
    (z : Fin r → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K))
    (hz : FormsPartOfRegularSystemOfParameters z) :
    r ≤ n ∧
      Nonempty
        ((MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K ⧸
            Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i => (z i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K)))) ≃ₐ[K]
          MvPowerSeries (Fin (n - r)) K) := by
  -- (a) `r ≤ n`: the `r` cotangent images of the `z_i` are linearly independent in the
  --     `n`-dimensional cotangent space (`finrank_cotangentSpace_field`), so
  --     `r = card (Fin r) ≤ finrank = n` by `LinearIndependent.fintype_card_le_finrank`.
  have hr : r ≤ n := by
    -- `LinearIndependent.fintype_card_le_finrank` + `finrank_cotangentSpace_field = n`.
    -- (Rewriting `Fintype.card (Fin r) = r`.)
    have hcard := hz.fintype_card_le_finrank
    rw [finrank_cotangentSpace_field, Fintype.card_fin] at hcard
    exact hcard
  refine ⟨hr, ?_⟩
  -- (b) Extend `z` to a full RSOP `z ++ w` (`extend_partial_rsop_field`), apply Statement
  --     (1) to get an automorphism `e` of `A` with `e (X i) = (z++w) i`. Then
  --     `A/(z_1..z_r) ≅ A/(e(X_0),…,e(X_{r-1})) = e(A/(X_0,…,X_{r-1}))`, and
  --     `A/(X_0,…,X_{r-1}) ≅ K[[Y_1..Y_{n-r}]]` by `quotient_initial_vars`.
  --     The `AlgEquiv` `e` carries `Ideal.span (range z)` to `Ideal.span (range (X∘castLE))`
  --     (since `e (X i) = z i` for `i < r`), giving the desired quotient iso by
  --     `Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq`/`Ideal.quotientEquiv` composed with
  --     `quotient_initial_vars`.
  classical
  obtain ⟨w, hrsp⟩ := extend_partial_rsop_field z hz hr
  exact nonempty_quotient_algEquiv_of_algEquiv_X hr z w
    (exists_algEquiv_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters K n _ hrsp)

/-! ### Normalization and translation over a Cohen ring (for statement (3))

Over a Cohen ring a member of a regular system of parameters need not have zero constant
coefficient: `y i = X i + p` is part of one, with `constantCoeff (y i) = ϖ ≠ 0`, so Mathlib's
substitution API does not apply to `y` itself. The normalization `ỹ i := y i - C (constantCoeff
(y i))` does have zero constant coefficients, so `substAlgHom` exists for `ỹ` and Engine 2
applies to it, and `(p, ỹ_1, …, ỹ_n)` is again a regular system of parameters; the desired
`e (X i) = y i` is then recovered by composing with the translation
`τ (X i) = X i + C (constantCoeff (y i))`. The normalization and its regular-system-of-parameters
invariance are the lemmas below; the translation factor is the `m_Λ`-adically convergent
`ShiftConstr.shiftAlgHom` of `MvPowerSeries.AdicTranslation`, packaged here as
`cohenTranslationAlgHom`. -/

/-- The constant coefficient of an element of the maximal ideal of `Λ[[x_σ]]` lies in
`m_Λ`. -/
theorem constantCoeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_mem_maximalIdeal {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ]
    [IsLocalRing Λ] {σ : Type*} (f : MvPowerSeries σ Λ)
    (hf : f ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries σ Λ)) :
    MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff f ∈ maximalIdeal Λ := by
  rw [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff, MvPowerSeries.isUnit_iff_constantCoeff] at hf
  rw [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff]
  exact hf

/-- An element of `Λ[[x_σ]]` minus its constant term lies in the maximal ideal: its constant
coefficient is zero. -/
theorem sub_C_constantCoeff_mem_maximalIdeal {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsLocalRing Λ]
    {σ : Type*} (f : MvPowerSeries σ Λ) :
    (f - MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff f)) ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries σ Λ) := by
  rw [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff, MvPowerSeries.isUnit_iff_constantCoeff,
    map_sub, MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff_C, sub_self]
  exact not_isUnit_zero

/-- The **normalization** `ỹ i := y i - C (constantCoeff (y i))` of a family `y` in `m_B`.
Each `ỹ i` again lies in `m_B` and has zero constant coefficient, so Mathlib's substitution
API applies to `ỹ`; and `y i = ỹ i + C (constantCoeff (y i))` recovers `y i` from `ỹ i` by a
translation by a constant whose coefficient lies in `m_Λ`. -/
noncomputable def normalizeCohen {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsLocalRing Λ] {σ : Type*}
    (y : σ → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries σ Λ)) :
    σ → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries σ Λ) := fun i =>
  ⟨(y i : MvPowerSeries σ Λ) -
      MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries σ Λ)),
    sub_C_constantCoeff_mem_maximalIdeal (y i : MvPowerSeries σ Λ)⟩

/-- The series underlying `normalizeCohen y i` is `y i` minus its constant term. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_normalizeCohen {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsLocalRing Λ] {σ : Type*}
    (y : σ → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries σ Λ)) (i : σ) :
    (normalizeCohen y i : MvPowerSeries σ Λ) =
      (y i : MvPowerSeries σ Λ) -
        MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries σ Λ)) :=
  rfl

/-- The normalized family has zero constant coefficients. -/
theorem constantCoeff_normalizeCohen {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsLocalRing Λ] {σ : Type*}
    (y : σ → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries σ Λ)) :
    ∀ i, MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (normalizeCohen y i : MvPowerSeries σ Λ) = (0 : Λ) :=
  fun i => by rw [coe_normalizeCohen, map_sub, MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff_C, sub_self]

/-- Adding back the constant term recovers `y i` from its normalization. -/
theorem normalizeCohen_add_C {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsLocalRing Λ] {σ : Type*}
    (y : σ → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries σ Λ)) (i : σ) :
    (normalizeCohen y i : MvPowerSeries σ Λ) +
        MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries σ Λ)) =
      (y i : MvPowerSeries σ Λ) := by
  rw [coe_normalizeCohen, sub_add_cancel]

/-- The cotangent map intertwines the ring scalar action with the residue-field scalar
action: `δ (b • x) = residue(b) • δ x` for `b : R` and `x ∈ m`. -/
theorem toCotangent_smul_residue {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] (b : R)
    (x : (maximalIdeal R)) :
    (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent (b • x) = residue R b • (maximalIdeal R).toCotangent x := by
  rw [map_smul, ←
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul (ResidueField R) b ((maximalIdeal R).toCotangent x)]
  rfl

/-- **Unipotent change of basis preserves bases.** If `V` is a basis (linearly independent
and spanning) of a `κ`-vector space `M`, `a 0 = 0`, and `W j = V j - a j • V 0`, then `W` is
also a basis. The forward map `V j ↦ V j - a j • V 0` is a linear automorphism (with explicit
inverse `V j ↦ V j + a j • V 0`), so it carries the basis `V` to a basis whose values are the
`W j`. -/
theorem linearIndependent_and_span_eq_top_of_sub_smul {κ : Type*} [CommRing κ] {M : Type*}
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module κ M] {N : ℕ} (V : Fin (N + 1) → M) (a : Fin (N + 1) → κ)
    (ha0 : a 0 = 0) (hli : LinearIndependent κ V) (hsp : Submodule.span κ (Set.range V) = ⊤)
    {W : Fin (N + 1) → M} (hW : ∀ j, W j = V j - a j • V 0) :
    LinearIndependent κ W ∧ Submodule.span κ (Set.range W) = ⊤ := by
  classical
  let bV : Module.Basis (Fin (N + 1)) κ M := Module.Basis.mk hli (by rw [hsp])
  have hbV : ∀ j, bV j = V j := fun j => Module.Basis.mk_apply hli _ j
  let f : M →ₗ[κ] M := bV.constr κ (fun j => V j - a j • V 0)
  let g : M →ₗ[κ] M := bV.constr κ (fun j => V j + a j • V 0)
  have hf : ∀ j, f (V j) = V j - a j • V 0 := by
    intro j
    have : f (bV j) = V j - a j • V 0 := Module.Basis.constr_basis bV κ _ j
    rwa [hbV j] at this
  have hg : ∀ j, g (V j) = V j + a j • V 0 := by
    intro j
    have : g (bV j) = V j + a j • V 0 := Module.Basis.constr_basis bV κ _ j
    rwa [hbV j] at this
  have hf0 : f (V 0) = V 0 := by rw [hf 0, ha0, zero_smul, sub_zero]
  have hg0 : g (V 0) = V 0 := by rw [hg 0, ha0, zero_smul, add_zero]
  have hfg : f.comp g = LinearMap.id := by
    apply bV.ext
    intro j
    rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.id_apply, hbV j, hg j, map_add, map_smul, hf j, hf0]
    abel_nf
  have hgf : g.comp f = LinearMap.id := by
    apply bV.ext
    intro j
    rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.id_apply, hbV j, hf j, map_sub, map_smul, hg j, hg0]
    abel_nf
  let e : M ≃ₗ[κ] M := LinearEquiv.ofLinearMap f g hfg hgf
  have he : ∀ x, e x = f x := fun x => rfl
  have hWe : ∀ j, W j = e (V j) := by
    intro j
    rw [hW j, he, hf j]
  let bW : Module.Basis (Fin (N + 1)) κ M := bV.map e
  have hbW : ∀ j, bW j = W j := by
    intro j
    rw [hWe j]
    show e (bV j) = e (V j)
    rw [hbV j]
  have hbWeq : (⇑bW) = W := funext hbW
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · have := bW.linearIndependent
    rwa [hbWeq] at this
  · have := bW.span_eq
    rwa [hbWeq] at this

/-- **Normalizing a regular system of parameters over a Cohen ring.** If `(p, y_1, …, y_n)`
is a regular system of parameters of `B = Λ[[x_1,…,x_n]]`, where `p = algebraMap ϖ` for a
generator `ϖ` of `m_Λ`, then so is `(p, ỹ_1, …, ỹ_n)` with
`ỹ i := y i - C (constantCoeff (y i))`.

Since `c_i := constantCoeff (y i) ∈ m_Λ = (ϖ)`, writing `c_i = ϖ · u_i` gives
`C c_i = p · C u_i`. In the cotangent space `δ (C c_i) = residue (C u_i) · δ p` (the `κ`-module
action on `Ideal.Cotangent`), so `δ (ỹ i) = δ (y i) − a_i · δ p` with `a_i := residue (C u_i)`.
This is a unipotent change of the basis `(δ p, δ y_1, …, δ y_n)` fixing `δ p`, with explicit
inverse `δ (y i) = δ (ỹ i) + a_i · δ p`; hence `(δ p, δ ỹ_1, …, δ ỹ_n)` is again a basis. -/
theorem isRegularSystemOfParameters_cons_normalizeCohen {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ]
    [IsLocalRing Λ] {n : ℕ} (ϖ : Λ) (hunif : maximalIdeal Λ = Ideal.span {ϖ})
    (p : maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (hp : (p : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) = algebraMap Λ (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) ϖ)
    (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (hrsp : IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.cons p y)) :
    IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.cons p (normalizeCohen y)) := by
  classical
  have hpC : (p : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) = MvPowerSeries.C ϖ := by
    simp [hp, MvPowerSeries.algebraMap_apply]
  have hc :
    ∀ i : Fin n, MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) ∈ maximalIdeal Λ :=
    fun i =>
      constantCoeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_mem_maximalIdeal (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) (y i).2
  have hdiv :
    ∀ i : Fin n,
      ∃ u : Λ, MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) = ϖ * u := by
    intro i
    obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.mp (hunif ▸ hc i)
    exact ⟨u, by rw [← hu, mul_comm]⟩
  choose u hu using hdiv
  -- the membership of the constant terms (as series) in the maximal ideal
  have hCmem :
    ∀ i : Fin n,
      MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) ∈
        maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) := by
    intro i
    simpa [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff,
      MvPowerSeries.isUnit_iff_constantCoeff] using hc i
  -- scalar function: 0 on the `p`-coordinate, `residue (C (u i))` on the `y_i`-coordinates.
  let a : Fin (n + 1) → ResidueField (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) :=
    Fin.cons 0 (fun i => residue (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) (MvPowerSeries.C (u i)))
  unfold IsRegularSystemOfParameters
  obtain ⟨hli, hsp⟩ := hrsp
  apply
    linearIndependent_and_span_eq_top_of_sub_smul
      (fun j =>
        (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)).toCotangent
          ((Fin.cons p y : Fin (n + 1) → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) j))
      a
  · -- a 0 = 0
    simp [a]
  · exact hli
  · exact hsp
  · -- W j = V j - a j • V 0
    intro j
    refine Fin.cases ?_ ?_ j
    · -- j = 0
      simp only [Fin.cons_zero]
      rw [show a 0 = 0 from by simp [a], zero_smul, sub_zero]
    · intro i
      -- j = i.succ
      simp only [Fin.cons_succ, Fin.cons_zero]
      change
        (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)).toCotangent
            ⟨(y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) -
                MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)),
              sub_C_constantCoeff_mem_maximalIdeal (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)⟩ =
          (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)).toCotangent (y i) -
            a i.succ • (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)).toCotangent p
      have ha : a i.succ = residue (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) (MvPowerSeries.C (u i)) := by simp [a]
      rw [ha]
      have hsub :
        (⟨(y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) -
                MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)),
              sub_C_constantCoeff_mem_maximalIdeal (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)⟩ :
            maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) =
          y i -
            ⟨MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)),
              hCmem i⟩ := by
        apply Subtype.ext; rfl
      rw [hsub, map_sub]
      congr 1
      have heq :
        (⟨MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)), hCmem i⟩ :
            maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) =
          (MvPowerSeries.C (u i) : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) • p := by
        apply Subtype.ext
        change
          MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) =
            MvPowerSeries.C (u i) * (p : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)
        rw [hpC, hu i, map_mul, mul_comm]
      rw [heq, toCotangent_smul_residue]

/-! ### The canonical substitution map of statement (3).

Over a Cohen ring the elements `y i ∈ m_B` of a regular system of parameters need NOT have
zero constant coefficient (`y i = X i + p` is a legitimate example), so Mathlib's
`MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom` — whose hypothesis `HasSubst` demands a *nilpotent* constant
coefficient, which fails in the domain `Λ` — cannot express the canonical map
`Λ[[Y_1,…,Y_n]] → B`, `Y_i ↦ y_i`. That map is nevertheless defined, by `m_B`-adic
convergence, and is realized here as `cohenSubstAlgHom`. -/

/-- The `m_Λ`-adic **translation** `X i ↦ X i + C (constantCoeff (y i))` of
`B = Λ[[x_1,…,x_n]]` attached to a family `y` in the maximal ideal `m_B`, over a Cohen ring
`Λ`. It is well defined because each constant coefficient lies in `m_Λ` and `Λ` is
`m_Λ`-adically complete. -/
noncomputable def cohenTranslationAlgHom {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsDomain Λ]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing Λ] (hΛ : IsCohenRing Λ) {n : ℕ}
    (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) :
    MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ →ₐ[Λ] MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ :=
  @ShiftConstr.shiftAlgHom Λ _ (maximalIdeal Λ) hΛ.isAdicComplete n
    (fun i => MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (fun i => constantCoeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_mem_maximalIdeal _ (y i).2)

/-- The translation sends `X i` to `X i + C (constantCoeff (y i))`. -/
@[simp]
theorem cohenTranslationAlgHom_X {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsDomain Λ]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing Λ] (hΛ : IsCohenRing Λ) {n : ℕ}
    (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) (i : Fin n) :
    cohenTranslationAlgHom hΛ y (MvPowerSeries.X i) =
      MvPowerSeries.X i +
        MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) :=
  @ShiftConstr.shiftAlgHom_X Λ _ (maximalIdeal Λ) hΛ.isAdicComplete n
    (fun i => MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (fun i => constantCoeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_mem_maximalIdeal _ (y i).2) i

/-- The translation is bijective: the opposite translation inverts it. -/
theorem cohenTranslationAlgHom_bijective {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsDomain Λ]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing Λ] (hΛ : IsCohenRing Λ) {n : ℕ}
    (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) :
    Function.Bijective (cohenTranslationAlgHom hΛ y) :=
  @ShiftConstr.shiftAlgHom_bijective Λ _ (maximalIdeal Λ) hΛ.isAdicComplete n
    (fun i => MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (fun i => constantCoeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_mem_maximalIdeal _ (y i).2)

/-- **The canonical substitution map** `Λ[[Y_1,…,Y_n]] → B = Λ[[x_1,…,x_n]]`, `Y_i ↦ y_i`,
of a family `y` in the maximal ideal `m_B`, over a Cohen ring `Λ`.

Writing `y i = ỹ i + C (c i)` with `c i = constantCoeff (y i) ∈ m_Λ` and `ỹ = normalizeCohen y`
(so `constantCoeff (ỹ i) = 0`), the map is the composite

  `Λ[[Y]] --(X i ↦ X i + C (c i))--> Λ[[Y]] --(X i ↦ ỹ i)--> B`,

the first factor being the `m_Λ`-adically convergent `cohenTranslationAlgHom`
(available because `Λ` is `m_Λ`-adically complete) and the second Mathlib's substitution
(available because `ỹ` has zero constant coefficients). Mathematically this composite is the
unique `m`-adically continuous `Λ`-algebra map sending `X i` to `y i`; that uniqueness
characterization is not formalized here — what is formalized is that this explicitly
constructed map does send `X i` to `y i` (`cohenSubstAlgHom_X`). -/
noncomputable def cohenSubstAlgHom {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsDomain Λ]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing Λ] (hΛ : IsCohenRing Λ) {n : ℕ}
    (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) :
    MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ →ₐ[Λ] MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ :=
  (MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom
        (MvPowerSeries.hasSubst_of_constantCoeff_zero (constantCoeff_normalizeCohen
            y))).comp (cohenTranslationAlgHom hΛ y)

/-- `cohenSubstAlgHom hΛ y f` is the substitution `X i ↦ normalizeCohen y i` applied to the
translate `cohenTranslationAlgHom hΛ y f`. -/
theorem cohenSubstAlgHom_apply {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsDomain Λ] [IsDiscreteValuationRing Λ]
    (hΛ : IsCohenRing Λ) {n : ℕ} (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (f : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) :
    cohenSubstAlgHom hΛ y f =
      MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom
          (MvPowerSeries.hasSubst_of_constantCoeff_zero (constantCoeff_normalizeCohen y))
        (cohenTranslationAlgHom hΛ y f) :=
  rfl

/-- The canonical map sends the variable `X i` to `y i`: it *is* the substitution
`Y_i ↦ y_i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem cohenSubstAlgHom_X {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsDomain Λ] [IsDiscreteValuationRing Λ]
    (hΛ : IsCohenRing Λ) {n : ℕ} (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) (i : Fin n) :
    cohenSubstAlgHom hΛ y (MvPowerSeries.X i) = (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) := by
  have hsub :=
    MvPowerSeries.hasSubst_of_constantCoeff_zero (constantCoeff_normalizeCohen y)
  have hC :
    (MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom hsub :
          MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ →ₐ[Λ] MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)
        (MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))) =
      MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) := by
    rw [MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom_apply, MvPowerSeries.subst_C]
  rw [cohenSubstAlgHom_apply, cohenTranslationAlgHom_X, map_add, MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom_X, hC]
  exact normalizeCohen_add_C y i

/-- **Statement (3), the isomorphism assertion.** The canonical substitution map is
bijective. Engine 2 gives this for the normalized family (whose substitution map is
Mathlib's `substAlgHom`), and the translation factor is invertible outright. -/
theorem cohenSubstAlgHom_bijective {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsDomain Λ]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing Λ] (hΛ : IsCohenRing Λ) {n : ℕ} (pr : ℕ)
    (hunif : maximalIdeal Λ = Ideal.span {(pr : Λ)})
    (p : maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (hp : (p : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) = algebraMap Λ (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) (pr : Λ))
    (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (hrsp : IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.cons p y)) :
    Function.Bijective (cohenSubstAlgHom hΛ y) := by
  -- `(p, ỹ)` is still a regular system of parameters (unipotent cotangent move).
  have hrsp' : IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.cons p (normalizeCohen y)) :=
    isRegularSystemOfParameters_cons_normalizeCohen (pr : Λ) hunif p hp y hrsp
  -- Engine 2 applies to the normalized family.
  have hbijsubst :
    Function.Bijective
      ((MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom
          (MvPowerSeries.hasSubst_of_constantCoeff_zero (constantCoeff_normalizeCohen y)) :
        MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ →ₐ[Λ] MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) :=
    ⟨engine_two_injective pr hunif p hp (normalizeCohen y) (constantCoeff_normalizeCohen y) hrsp',
      engine_two_surjective pr hunif p hp (normalizeCohen y) (constantCoeff_normalizeCohen y)
        hrsp'⟩
  exact hbijsubst.comp (cohenTranslationAlgHom_bijective hΛ y)

/-- **Statement (3).** Let `Lambda` be a Cohen ring with uniformizer the prime number
`pr`, and let `B = Lambda[[x_1, ..., x_n]]`. If `p, y_1, ..., y_n` is a regular system of
parameters of `B` (where `p = pr` viewed in `B` via the coefficient inclusion), then the
canonical `Lambda`-algebra homomorphism `Lambda[[Y_1, ..., Y_n]] -> B` sending `Y_i` to
`y_i` — `cohenSubstAlgHom`, the `m_Λ`-adic translation followed by substitution of the
normalized family — is an isomorphism: it sends `X i` to `y i` and it is bijective. -/
@[stacks 07NM "(3)", sga "1 III 2.3" "special case"]
theorem main_theorem_three (Λ : Type*) [CommRing Λ] [IsDomain Λ] [IsDiscreteValuationRing Λ]
    (hΛ : IsCohenRing Λ) (n : ℕ) (pr : ℕ) (hunif : maximalIdeal Λ = Ideal.span {(pr : Λ)})
    (p : maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (hp : (p : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) = algebraMap Λ (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) (pr : Λ))
    (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (hrsp : IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.cons p y)) :
    (∀ i, cohenSubstAlgHom hΛ y (MvPowerSeries.X i) = (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ)) ∧
      Function.Bijective (cohenSubstAlgHom hΛ y) :=
  ⟨cohenSubstAlgHom_X hΛ y, cohenSubstAlgHom_bijective hΛ pr hunif p hp y hrsp⟩

/-- Statement (3) repackaged as an automorphism: the canonical map, being bijective, is a
`Λ`-algebra automorphism of `B` carrying `X i` to `y i`. This existential form is strictly
weaker than `main_theorem_three` (it forgets which map it is); it is the form in which
statement (4) consumes (3). -/
theorem exists_algEquiv_of_isRegularSystemOfParameters_cohen (Λ : Type*) [CommRing Λ] [IsDomain Λ]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing Λ] (hΛ : IsCohenRing Λ) (n : ℕ) (pr : ℕ)
    (hunif : maximalIdeal Λ = Ideal.span {(pr : Λ)})
    (p : maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (hp : (p : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) = algebraMap Λ (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) (pr : Λ))
    (y : Fin n → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (hrsp : IsRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.cons p y)) :
    ∃ e : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ ≃ₐ[Λ] MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ,
      ∀ i, e (MvPowerSeries.X i) = (y i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ) :=
  ⟨AlgEquiv.ofBijective _ (main_theorem_three Λ hΛ n pr hunif p hp y hrsp).2,
    (main_theorem_three Λ hΛ n pr hunif p hp y hrsp).1⟩

/-- Cohen analogue of `extend_partial_rsop_field`. Given `z_1,…,z_r` such that the
length-`(r+1)` family `(p, z_1,…,z_r)` has linearly-independent cotangent images
(`FormsPartOfRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.cons p z)`), there exist `w_1,…,w_{n-r}`
such that `(p, z_1,…,z_r, w_1,…,w_{n-r})` is a full regular system of parameters of
`B = Λ[[x_1,…,x_n]]`. The cotangent space has dimension `n+1` here (the extra `+1`
coming from the prepended uniformizer `p`). -/
theorem extend_partial_rsop_cohen {Λ : Type*} [CommRing Λ] [IsDomain Λ] [IsDiscreteValuationRing Λ]
    (hΛ : IsCohenRing Λ) {n r : ℕ} (p : maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (z : Fin r → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ))
    (hz : IsPartOfRegularSystemOfParameters (Fin.cons p z)) (hr : r ≤ n) :
    ∃ w : Fin (n - r) → maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ),
      IsRegularSystemOfParameters
        (Fin.cons p (Fin.append z w ∘ Fin.cast (by omega : n = r + (n - r)))) := by
  classical
  set B := MvPowerSeries (Fin n) Λ
  -- The cotangent space is finite-dimensional (no global instance; obtain from a basis).
  have : Module.Finite (ResidueField B) (CotangentSpace B) := by
    obtain ⟨bas⟩ := nonempty_basis_cotangentSpace_cohen (Λ := Λ) hΛ (n := n)
    exact Module.Finite.of_basis bas
  -- Unfold the hypothesis to a bare `LinearIndependent` statement.
  unfold IsPartOfRegularSystemOfParameters at hz
  -- The prepended length-`(r+1)` family `u = (p, z_1,…,z_r)` and its cotangent images `v`.
  set u : Fin (r + 1) → maximalIdeal B := Fin.cons p z with hu
  set v : Fin (r + 1) → CotangentSpace B := fun i => (maximalIdeal B).toCotangent (u i)
  have hindv : LinearIndependent (ResidueField B) v := hz
  -- Span of `v` and a complement `W`.
  set S : Submodule (ResidueField B) (CotangentSpace B) :=
    Submodule.span (ResidueField B) (Set.range v) with hS
  obtain ⟨W, hW⟩ := S.exists_isCompl
  -- Dimensions: `finrank V = n+1`, `finrank S = r+1`, hence `finrank W = n - r`.
  have hfinV : Module.finrank (ResidueField B) (CotangentSpace B) = n + 1 :=
    finrank_cotangentSpace_cohen hΛ
  have hfinS : Module.finrank (ResidueField B) S = r + 1 := by
    rw [hS, finrank_span_eq_card hindv, Fintype.card_fin]
  have hfinW : Module.finrank (ResidueField B) W = n - r := by
    have hadd := Submodule.finrank_add_eq_of_isCompl hW
    rw [hfinS, hfinV] at hadd
    omega
  -- A basis of `W` indexed by `Fin (n - r)`, viewed in `V`.
  set bW : Module.Basis (Fin (n - r)) (ResidueField B) W :=
    Module.finBasisOfFinrankEq (ResidueField B) W hfinW
  set bW' : Fin (n - r) → CotangentSpace B := fun j => (bW j : CotangentSpace B) with hbW'
  -- Lift each basis vector of `W` to an element of `m` via surjectivity of `toCotangent`.
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (maximalIdeal B).toCotangent :=
    Ideal.toCotangent_surjective (maximalIdeal B)
  set w : Fin (n - r) → maximalIdeal B := fun j => (hsurj (bW' j)).choose
  have hwspec : ∀ j, (maximalIdeal B).toCotangent (w j) = bW' j := fun j =>
    (hsurj (bW' j)).choose_spec
  refine ⟨w, ?_⟩
  unfold IsRegularSystemOfParameters
  -- Reindex: `Fin.cons p (Fin.append z w ∘ Fin.cast h) = Fin.append u w ∘ Fin.cast h'`.
  have hcons :
    (Fin.cons p (Fin.append z w ∘ Fin.cast (by omega : n = r + (n - r)))) =
      Fin.append u w ∘
        Fin.cast (by omega : r + 1 + (n - r) = r + 1 + (n - r)) ∘
        Fin.cast (by omega : n + 1 = r + 1 + (n - r)) := by
    funext i
    refine Fin.cases ?_ ?_ i
    · simp only [Fin.cons_zero, Function.comp_apply, hu]
      have hidx :
        (Fin.cast (by omega : n + 1 = r + 1 + (n - r)) 0) =
          Fin.castAdd (n - r) (0 : Fin (r + 1)) := by
        apply Fin.ext; simp
      rw [Fin.cast_cast, hidx, Fin.append_left, Fin.cons_zero]
    · intro j
      simp only [Fin.cons_succ, Function.comp_apply, hu]
      by_cases hj : (j : ℕ) < r
      · have hidxL :
          (Fin.cast (by omega : n = r + (n - r)) j) = Fin.castAdd (n - r) ⟨(j : ℕ), hj⟩ := by
          apply Fin.ext; simp
        rw [hidxL, Fin.append_left]
        have hidxR :
          (Fin.cast (by omega : n + 1 = r + 1 + (n - r)) j.succ) =
            Fin.castAdd (n - r) (⟨(j : ℕ) + 1, by omega⟩ : Fin (r + 1)) := by
          apply Fin.ext; simp [Fin.val_succ]
        rw [Fin.cast_cast, hidxR, Fin.append_left]
        rw [show (⟨(j : ℕ) + 1, by omega⟩ : Fin (r + 1)) = (⟨(j : ℕ), hj⟩ : Fin r).succ from by
            apply Fin.ext; simp []]
        rw [Fin.cons_succ]
      · have hidxL :
          (Fin.cast (by omega : n = r + (n - r)) j) = Fin.natAdd r ⟨(j : ℕ) - r, by omega⟩ := by
          apply Fin.ext; simp; omega
        rw [hidxL, Fin.append_right]
        have hidxR :
          (Fin.cast (by omega : n + 1 = r + 1 + (n - r)) j.succ) =
            Fin.natAdd (r + 1) ⟨(j : ℕ) - r, by omega⟩ := by
          apply Fin.ext; simp [Fin.val_succ]; omega
        rw [Fin.cast_cast, hidxR, Fin.append_right]
  -- The cotangent images of the combined family `Fin.append u w`.
  have happend :
    (fun i => (maximalIdeal B).toCotangent (Fin.append u w i)) = Fin.append v bW' := by
    funext i
    refine Fin.addCases ?_ ?_ i
    · intro k; simp only [Fin.append_left]; rfl
    · intro k; simp only [Fin.append_right]; exact hwspec k
  -- Linear independence of `bW'` and its span = `W`.
  have hindbW' : LinearIndependent (ResidueField B) bW' := by
    rw [hbW']
    exact bW.linearIndependent.map' W.subtype (by simp)
  have hspanbW' : Submodule.span (ResidueField B) (Set.range bW') = W := by
    have hrng : Set.range bW' = (W.subtype) '' (Set.range bW) := by
      rw [hbW']; rw [← Set.range_comp]; rfl
    rw [hrng, Submodule.span_image]
    simp [bW.span_eq]
  -- Disjointness of the two spans.
  have hdisj :
    Disjoint (Submodule.span (ResidueField B) (Set.range v))
      (Submodule.span (ResidueField B) (Set.range bW')) := by
    rw [hspanbW']
    have hvS : Submodule.span (ResidueField B) (Set.range v) = S := hS.symm
    rw [hvS]
    exact hW.disjoint
  -- Combine into a single linearly-independent family `Fin.append v bW'`.
  have hsum : LinearIndependent (ResidueField B) (Sum.elim v bW') :=
    LinearIndependent.sum_type hindv hindbW' hdisj
  have happ : Fin.append v bW' = Sum.elim v bW' ∘ finSumFinEquiv.symm := by
    have hcomp : Fin.append v bW' ∘ finSumFinEquiv = Sum.elim v bW' := by
      ext x
      cases x with
      | inl a =>
        simp only [Function.comp_apply, finSumFinEquiv_apply_left, Fin.append_left, Sum.elim_inl]
      | inr a =>
        simp only [Function.comp_apply, finSumFinEquiv_apply_right, Fin.append_right, Sum.elim_inr]
    rw [← hcomp]; ext x; simp
  have hindapp : LinearIndependent (ResidueField B) (Fin.append v bW') := by
    rw [happ]; exact hsum.comp _ finSumFinEquiv.symm.injective
  -- The cotangent images of the full family, as `Fin.append v bW' ∘ cast`.
  set g : Fin (n + 1) → CotangentSpace B := fun i =>
    (maximalIdeal B).toCotangent
      ((Fin.cons p (Fin.append z w ∘ Fin.cast (by omega : n = r + (n - r))) :
          Fin (n + 1) → maximalIdeal B)
        i) with
    hg
  have hgeq : g = Fin.append v bW' ∘ Fin.cast (by omega : n + 1 = r + 1 + (n - r)) := by
    funext i
    simp only [hg, hcons, Function.comp_apply]
    have :=
      congrFun happend
        (Fin.cast (by omega : r + 1 + (n - r) = r + 1 + (n - r))
          (Fin.cast (by omega : n + 1 = r + 1 + (n - r)) i))
    simpa [Fin.cast_cast] using this
  -- Linear independence of `g`.
  have hindg : LinearIndependent (ResidueField B) g := by
    rw [hgeq]
    exact hindapp.comp _ (Fin.cast_injective _)
  -- Assemble: independence + span = ⊤ (card `n+1` = finrank).
  refine ⟨hindg, ?_⟩
  have hcard :
    Fintype.card (Fin (n + 1)) = Module.finrank (ResidueField B) (CotangentSpace B) := by
    rw [Fintype.card_fin, hfinV]
  exact hindg.span_eq_top_of_card_eq_finrank hcard

/-- **Statement (4).** Let `Lambda` be a Cohen ring with uniformizer the prime number
`pr`, and let `B = Lambda[[x_1, ..., x_n]]`. If `p, z_1, ..., z_r` form part of a regular
system of parameters for `B` (the length-`(r+1)` sequence `p, z_1, ..., z_r`, with `p`
the uniformizer viewed in `B`), then `r <= n` and `B/(z_1, ..., z_r)` is isomorphic (as a
`Lambda`-algebra) to the power series ring `Lambda[[Y_1, ..., Y_{n-r}]]`. -/
